# domains.conf.example
# Author: ungentilgarcon (assisted by GitHub Copilot / Copilot CLI)
# License: GPL-3.0-or-later - see LICENSE at the repository root
#
# One certificate per line. The first domain on a line is the certificate's
# primary name (what acme.sh stores it under, e.g. ~/.acme.sh/<primary>/);
# any further domains on the same line become additional SANs on that same
# certificate. Blank lines and lines starting with # are ignored.
#
# Copy this file to e.g. ~/acme-scripts/domains.conf and edit it, then run:
#   ./renew-multi.sh --config ~/acme-scripts/domains.conf
#
# Examples:

# Single domain, no SAN:
example.com

# Domain + apex/www SAN pair:
example2.com www.example2.com

# Wildcard + apex in the same certificate (needs DNS-01, which is what
# dns_orange.sh provides):
example3.com *.example3.com

# A completely unrelated domain can be on the same line too - acme.sh
# doesn't require SANs to share a parent zone, and dns_orange.sh looks up
# the correct Orange DNS hosted zone independently for each name:
example4.com www.example4.com *.example4.com
